        <mxCell id="legend" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4F6F7;strokeColor=#7F8C8D;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=18;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#34495E;shadow=0;" value="&lt;b&gt;Viewpoint&lt;/b&gt;  decomposition of one deployment box: Splunk Operator (SOK)  ·  square on boundary = facade port traced from deployment communication&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;UML notation&lt;/b&gt;  every subcomponent relationship uses a named native Provided/Required Interface assembly  ·  solid arrowless component-to-port line = delegation  ·  dashed open arrow = external «use» dependency only (client → supplier)  ·  no bare component joins are used&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Theme&lt;/b&gt;  Teal = existing SOK/Splunk  ·  Teal + orange outline = existing component changed for ITSI  ·  Orange = new ITSI logic  ·  Gray = external/stock&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Scope&lt;/b&gt;  PodExecClientImpl and ControllerClient are implementation interfaces. Every repeated PodExec interface is labeled RunPodExecCommand. ITSI entry interfaces map one-to-one to the exact code methods shown beside them on branch feature/itsi-app-framework-s1-c3-minimal. Internal method assemblies use exact callable names; «use» is reserved for external systems. License handling, Java, upgrade, build pipeline and downstream propagation are outside this view." vertex="1">
